--- doc/trace.n
+++ doc/trace.n
@@ -199,10 +199,18 @@
 parenthesized index).  If \fIname\fR refers to a whole array, then
 \fIcommandPrefix\fR is invoked whenever any element of the array is
 manipulated.  If the variable does not exist, it will be created but
 will not be given a value, so it will be visible to \fBnamespace which\fR
 queries, but not to \fBinfo exists\fR queries.
+Such a variable is not an array yet: reading an element of it fails with a
+.QW "no such variable"
+error without invoking a \fBread\fR trace set on \fIname\fR.
+Traces on a whole array are invoked for its elements only once the
+variable is an array, for example after an element has been written or
+after \fBarray set\fR \fIname\fR \fB{}\fR.
+(A trace set on a single element, such as \fBa(x)\fR, makes the variable
+an array.)
